{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-161445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y<1-x}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/5151df3c5b84ffaca9aa16b401cd9364fea10a240d39c9c28d815b36e417b16d.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains none of its boundary points. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we've seen, $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ contains none of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A=A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161445" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3ae459cea8d84b726fb17483f9d3c292ea3262f8b4761f518b942f77507b58e"} {"question" "q-161445" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161445" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true."]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161445" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the set $A,$ defined by \n\n$$\nA={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,1<{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 4}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n- $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n- $\\text{int}\\,A=A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nIn this case, the set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8414de2e05da43c03fae3c8b1ff2102401e990188e9fd4ee59a24308ec34b086.png)\n\n \n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nNotice that, in this case, the set $A$ contains some (not all) of its boundary points.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement:\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. As we have seen, $∂A$ consists of two concentric circles: the outer one is in $A,$ while the inner one is not.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ contains some of its boundary points, we must have $\\text{int}\\,A\\ne A.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161624" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3ae459cea8d84b726fb17483f9d3c292ea3262f8b4761f518b942f77507b58e"} {"question" "q-161624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161624" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/af1e6e7b384732a527fc77e9729c6e02aaa288d4076c030c9fae58742cb10f74.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/0a0b92621d83d6395926a75b5cae34f479a8b9e64dfe82711094c3724b3b3220.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/3ddef68bf4b4284c1b68896920fddb8d7fb0e70eba15dee103cdbc0134a9ed20.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<2,\\,-x<y<x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161718" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3ae459cea8d84b726fb17483f9d3c292ea3262f8b4761f518b942f77507b58e"} {"question" "q-161718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-x<y<x"] ["math" "-x\\le y<x"] ["math" "-x\\le y\\le x"] ["math" "0<y<x"] ["math" "0<y\\le x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161718" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-x<y<x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/aa335a55f5b4496cdaccca5d35e286a168598761188bc520c81397ef136f927d.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/fba9ba3e52ed19eb0bb2286ae59c49bb9dc648134d9eab3c4e2d13862963f736.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/2f3cd30dbaa4f84c43f2a7f1197aa904e3d43b1212241ae26736b2a0087f6170.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<4,\\,0<y<2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3ae459cea8d84b726fb17483f9d3c292ea3262f8b4761f518b942f77507b58e"} {"question" "q-161730" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161730" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1\\le y\\le 1"] ["math" "0<y<2"] ["math" "0\\le y\\le 2"] ["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161730" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0<y<2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8d7ceac8c936a745ae79f71844a6d1a74175b1b97a2a497588d34c9ff988cdf9.png)\n\nConsider the set $A$ shown above. The interior of $A$ is \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/c0e6ef400b15c54264a400af99bef64c3bb5aeb7ceadbdd599375c0f1e0d3642.png)\n\nThe interior of a set $A,$ denoted $\\text{int}\\,A,$ is the set containing all the interior points of $A.$ It contains every point in $A$ except the boundary points: \n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A=A-∂A\n$$\n\nThe interior of $A$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/assets/8c5bbdfca6736194791f834ab4aadb03a30e3f116e89ffd5a7ea3e0104708ae4.png)\n\nSo, in this case, the interior of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{int}\\,A={(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0<x<3,\\,0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161731" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c3ae459cea8d84b726fb17483f9d3c292ea3262f8b4761f518b942f77507b58e"} {"question" "q-161731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}x<y<0"] ["math" "0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x"] ["math" "0\\le y\\le \\frac{2}{3}x"] ["math" "y=0"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{3}x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"} {"question" "q-161731" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0<y<\\frac{2}{3}x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14053801/state.json" "file_sha256" "94ac63a9126886f474789f078c3a1c5685d23a0d9531141c7d088768d6862028"}] "usage" {"q-161445" []} "basis" 1806 "retractions" [[17592186193040 :question/problem "Consider the set $A$, defined by\n$A = {(x, y) ∈ R^{2}: y < 1 - x}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $A$ contains all of its boundary points.\n2. $A$ contains none of its boundary points.\n3. $intA = A$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186191090 17592186191091 17592186191092 17592186191093 17592186191094] "immutable_fields" [[17592186191089 :answer-field/correct] [17592186191089 :answer-field/id] [17592186191089 :answer-field/key] [17592186191089 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
